{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"const DetachableRunCapability: Capability<true, \"detachable-run\">;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L322","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:322"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether the current run can be DETACHED rather than destroyed when its client\ndisconnects — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" only when some middleware has both a "},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/RunStore.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"RunStore"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and\na durable event log wired ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":"'s "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runs"},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"durability.adapter"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lives in core for the same reason "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LockStore"},{"type":"text","value":" does: it is a coordination fact\nthat two consumer packages must agree on, and neither may depend on the other.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-sandbox"},{"type":"text","value":" provides it; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-persistence"},{"type":"text","value":" reads it to\ndecide whether an abort is terminal ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'aborted'"},{"type":"text","value":") or a detach (write nothing).\nA persistence → sandbox import would be a layering inversion."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Consumers read it with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ optional: true }"},{"type":"text","value":": absent means \"not detachable\",\nwhich is every app that has not wired durability."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", not "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"},{"type":"text","value":": ABSENCE is the negative, so a published "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":"\nhas no meaning — and a consumer that tests PRESENCE rather than the value\nwould read one as \"detachable\". Narrowing the payload makes that\nunrepresentable instead of merely undocumented."}]}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nconst DetachableRunCapability: Capability<true, \"detachable-run\">;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:322](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L322)\n\nWhether the current run can be DETACHED rather than destroyed when its client\ndisconnects — `true` only when some middleware has both a [RunStore](../interfaces/RunStore.md) and\na durable event log wired (`withSandbox`'s `runs` + `durability.adapter`).\n\nLives in core for the same reason `LockStore` does: it is a coordination fact\nthat two consumer packages must agree on, and neither may depend on the other.\n`@tanstack/ai-sandbox` provides it; `@tanstack/ai-persistence` reads it to\ndecide whether an abort is terminal (`'aborted'`) or a detach (write nothing).\nA persistence → sandbox import would be a layering inversion.\n\nConsumers read it with `{ optional: true }`: absent means \"not detachable\",\nwhich is every app that has not wired durability.\n\nTyped `true`, not `boolean`: ABSENCE is the negative, so a published `false`\nhas no meaning — and a consumer that tests PRESENCE rather than the value\nwould read one as \"detachable\". Narrowing the payload makes that\nunrepresentable instead of merely undocumented.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: DetachableRunCapability\ntitle: DetachableRunCapability\n---\n\n```ts\nconst DetachableRunCapability: Capability<true, \"detachable-run\">;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:322](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L322)\n\nWhether the current run can be DETACHED rather than destroyed when its client\ndisconnects — `true` only when some middleware has both a [RunStore](../interfaces/RunStore.md) and\na durable event log wired (`withSandbox`'s `runs` + `durability.adapter`).\n\nLives in core for the same reason `LockStore` does: it is a coordination fact\nthat two consumer packages must agree on, and neither may depend on the other.\n`@tanstack/ai-sandbox` provides it; `@tanstack/ai-persistence` reads it to\ndecide whether an abort is terminal (`'aborted'`) or a detach (write nothing).\nA persistence → sandbox import would be a layering inversion.\n\nConsumers read it with `{ optional: true }`: absent means \"not detachable\",\nwhich is every app that has not wired durability.\n\nTyped `true`, not `boolean`: ABSENCE is the negative, so a published `false`\nhas no meaning — and a consumer that tests PRESENCE rather than the value\nwould read one as \"detachable\". Narrowing the payload makes that\nunrepresentable instead of merely undocumented.\n"}
